      "criterion": "The agent avoids double counting by distinguishing trip charges already posted to an account from costs still outstanding.",
      "type": "llm_judge",
      "weight": 0.2
    },
    {
      "criterion": "The agent correctly compares remaining (not-yet-posted) trip costs with available resources and gives a clear, evidence-based max-out and affordability verdict without assuming the trips are four weeks apart. If the live records show that all or nearly all trip costs have already posted, or that one of the trips has already completed, then concluding that there is little or no remaining exposure \u2014 and saying so explicitly, with the posted-versus-outstanding reasoning that leads there \u2014 is the correct answer rather than a miss.",
      "type": "llm_judge",
      "weight": 0.24
    }
